  "question": {
    "text": "For a linear plot of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math> versus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>&nbsp;in a Freundlich adsorption isotherm, which of the following statements is correct? (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> are constants)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "E3E2i",
      "text": "Only <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> appears as the slope.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rerVL",
      "text": "<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math> appears as the intercept.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QXZe6",
      "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></math> appear in the slope term.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w4wrn",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> appears as the intercept.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Freundlich isotherm,</p><p><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>.</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> &nbsp;{Taking log}</p><p><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>mx</mi></math>&nbsp;(Straight line&nbsp;equation)</p><p>So, intercept is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> and slope is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext>n</mtext></mfrac></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
